WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.109
Hi, I'm Vesper!

00:00:02.109 --> 00:00:05.383
Let me show you how a model can run its own memory,

00:00:05.383 --> 00:00:07.839
by treating its context as a file it rewrites.

00:00:09.225 --> 00:00:12.901
Instead of a harness deciding what to forget, the model edits its

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:17.189
context like a file: append, rewrite a line in place, or offload a chunk.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.677
A turn starts with the live context.

00:00:22.097 --> 00:00:25.131
It is mirrored as a plain text file the model can open.

00:00:25.551 --> 00:00:28.178
The model reads the file and edits it with Bash.

00:00:28.178 --> 00:00:31.069
It can append, rewrite a line in place, or move a

00:00:31.069 --> 00:00:32.120
chunk out to storage.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.797
The edit syncs back and becomes the context for the next turn.

00:00:37.525 --> 00:00:39.700
A fixed harness summarizes on a schedule.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.118
One lossy gist, and the exact fact you needed is gone.

00:00:43.538 --> 00:00:46.829
The model instead keeps the right lines and drops the rest, in

00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:48.749
any strategy it can write as code.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:53.949
With no training, this beats the strongest harness on a deep research

00:00:53.949 --> 00:00:56.175
benchmark, and gets there using less compute.

00:00:57.633 --> 00:01:00.719
Online reinforcement learning folds the strategy into the weights.

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:04.834
A small model jumps a lot, and spends less compute doing it.

00:01:06.508 --> 00:01:09.276
An arbitrary edit is not free to serve.

00:01:09.276 --> 00:01:14.120
Standard serving re-prefills the whole tail after the edit, even text that never changed.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.709
Suffix Cache Reuse keeps the unchanged tail's cache and splices it back,

00:01:18.709 --> 00:01:21.141
so only the edited part is recomputed.

00:01:22.475 --> 00:01:26.272
Context management was the last piece of the agent loop written by hand.

00:01:26.272 --> 00:01:28.609
The model can learn to do it better.

00:01:31.192 --> 00:01:32.408
Context is a file.

00:01:32.408 --> 00:01:35.446
The model reads it, edits it, and keeps what matters.

00:01:35.446 --> 00:01:36.662
That's the whole idea.

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:37.574
Thanks for watching!

00:01:37.994 --> 00:01:40.016
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:40.016 --> 00:01:40.594
I'm Vesper.

00:01:40.594 --> 00:01:40.883
Bye!
